 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you? Start it on dry surface nearby, and only switch the damp wood once it's really going. Also, keep a dry blanket nearby. Yes, they're great for starting a small fire. Roughly the amount of space between the threads is how much space you need for air. Pack them tightly, no air pockets, and put them in a ziplock bag. Big enough that it's easy to see the flames, but not so big that it gets out of hand. Stick to one pot at first, and buy a heat mat and thermostat if you' unsure. Set it on a wire mesh tray on top of a heat mat, and cover it with a thin heat mat pad. Turn it off before pulling the blanket over.",
